SINGLEPLAYER OOM LEAK (physics-frozen + RAM-grows-until-OOM, terrain demo) ROOT CAUSE + FIX (commit 0313d952): NOT a texture/static allocation (those cuts didn't fix it) and NOT server-side (node ws server RSS was STABLE at 177MB with a connected player - decisive bisection). It is the SINGLEPLAYER worker->main postMessage SNAPSHOT channel. The worker (BrowserServer's Web Worker = the authoritative server) ticks + posts a snapshot at the server rate (~32Hz after the 2Hz->32Hz _computeSnapshotInterval smoothing fix). client/BrowserServer.js worker.onmessage processed EVERY snapshot synchronously; when the main thread renders below 32fps (heavy mapspinner planet raymarch frame), processing can't keep up -> the worker->main postMessage queue grows UNBOUNDED (each held snapshot ArrayBuffer) -> RAM climbs to OOM while the displayed state lags further every second (the 'physics frozen' symptom; it's the render/consume loop starving, not the worker sim). The 32Hz smoothing made it ~16x faster than the old 2Hz (why it surfaced 'since physics was smoothed'). FIX: snapshots are idempotent (latest wins) so COALESCE - WorkerTransport.send tags each post with mt=message-type (threaded via ConnectionManager.send/broadcast + TransportWrapper.sendUnreliable), and BrowserServer.onmessage keeps only the LATEST snapshot (mt===MSG.SNAPSHOT 0x10), processing it once per requestAnimationFrame; the cheap store drains the postMessage queue immediately so it can never back up. Non-snapshot msgs (worldDef, app events, STATE_CORRECTION/RECOVERY) stay immediate + never dropped. Multiplayer (ws PhysicsNetworkClient) path unaffected (WebSocketTransport doesn't tag mt -> no coalesce, and ws backpressure differs). Witness: localhost SP connects through the coalesced flush (client.connected=true via the rAF flush, _snapScheduled active); netcode tests 12/12. CAVEAT: a per-frame/per-message client leak is INVISIBLE on the node server (server stable) - bisect SP-vs-MP by watching server RSS with a connected player before blaming the sim.